{
  "suite": "verdict",
  "methodologyVersion": "1.5.0",
  "fixtureSchemaVersion": 2,
  "decisionRules": [
    {
      "id": "compliance/exact-binomial",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "regression/fisher",
      "version": 1
    }
  ],
  "description": "Verdict evaluation under the two ruled rules: regression/fisher for a baseline-derived threshold and compliance/exact-binomial for a given one; each case names its rule in decisionRule. A test carrying a requirement and a baseline on the same postconditions (approach two_criteria) carries two criteria over the same observations, a compliance criterion and a regression criterion, each with one rule and one alpha (compliance_alpha, regression_alpha) and one verdict, reported in criteria; the test's verdict is their structural composite (PASS if both pass, FAIL if either fails, INCONCLUSIVE otherwise), triggering_criteria names the criteria that decided it, and the error envelopes are split by direction. The test is refused whole when any part is invalid, reporting every applicable code. The v1.4.1 point-estimate rule (PASS iff p_hat >= threshold) and its Wald z statistic are withdrawn. Binding: verdict, configuration_error, criteria, triggering_criteria. Informational: observed_rate, false_compliance_envelope, false_degradation_signal_envelope.",
  "method": "regression/fisher: PASS iff K_t >= c(K_b, n_b, n_t, alpha) (see regression_decision). compliance/exact-binomial: PASS iff K >= k_min(p_req, n, alpha) (see compliance_decision). Configuration errors are checked first, for every part of the configuration; configuration_error is the list of every applicable code in the fixed order TEST_LARGER_THAN_BASELINE, COMPLIANCE_INFEASIBLE (empty when valid).",
  "tolerance": 1e-10,
